<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea May agricultural import prices down - AFTAK.</title>
<headline>S.Korea May agricultural import prices down - AFTAK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's agricultural commodities import prices fell in May from the previous month on losses in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>However, coffee import prices surged on supply concerns at major producing countries and low stockpiles in leading consumer countries, it said.</p>
<p>AFTAK, established in 1970, has 13,200 members representing more than 45,000 overseas suppliers.</p>
<p>Its member firms handle over 82 percent of the country's total imports.  </p>
<p>May import prices for agricultural commodities were as follows:</p>
<p>(US$ price per tonne on C&amp;F)</p>
<p> COMMODITY   TYPE			 ORIGIN     May    Apr</p>
<p> Wheat	 Soft White		 U.S.	 196    201</p>
<p> Wheat	 Hard Red Winter	  U.S.	 202    219</p>
<p> Wheat	 Dark Northern Spring   U.S.	 207    221</p>
<p> Corn	  No.3 yellow		U.S.	 138    145</p>
<p> Soybean     No.2			 U.S.	 342    350</p>
<p> Soymeal				    U.S.	 320    330</p>
<p> Tallow	TW (FOB)		   U.S.	 460    440</p>
<p> Palm oil    Olein (FOB)		Malaysia   575    590</p>
<p> Sugar	 96-97 pct		  Thailand   295    305</p>
<p> Coffee	NY No.2 (FOB)	    Brazil   4,994  4,220</p>
<p> Rubber	RSS No.3		   Malaysia 1,147  1,125</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
